---
description: Avoid AI-style punctuation and mirrored wording in prose output
alwaysApply: true
---

# Plain prose (always on)

Applies to agent chat, comments, commits, docs, and PR text. Does not change caveman chat compression; it only blocks dash-heavy phrasing and copying AI tells from context.

## Banned in prose you write

Do not emit these as clause connectors or dramatic pauses:

- Em dash (U+2014)
- En dash (U+2013) between words or clauses
- Horizontal bar (U+2015)
- Spaced hyphen used as a pause (` - `)
- Double hyphen used as a pause (`--`)

## Rewrite, do not swap

When a sentence would use a dash, recast it: split into two sentences, or use a comma, colon, or parentheses. Do not replace a dash with another dash-like character.

Before finishing a user-visible prose reply, scan for U+2014, U+2013, and U+2015 and rewrite any hit.

## Do not mirror context

If pasted text, quotes, tool output, or prior instructions use em dashes, en dashes, or stock AI phrasing, do not echo that wording. State the same fact in plain sentences.

## Exceptions

Keep these characters only where they are required or verbatim:

- Code, string literals, regex, and Unicode escapes
- Direct quotations that already contain the character (do not add dashes to quotes)
